-----------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS DID NOT MEASURE, and it is the one thing it was run for
-----------------------------------------------------------------
The cost box is HIDDEN in both fixture sets. Neither carries
`cost/<env>/latest.json`, so `renderCostLine()` finds nothing to say and
leaves the box with its `hidden` attribute - which is the correct
behaviour and means its height was never on the page being measured.

So "+0 on every desktop viewport" is NOT "the cost box costs nothing".
It is "the cost box was not there". The distinction is the empty result
that looks clean, arriving from the fixtures rather than from the tool.

-----------------------------------------------------------------
THE PHONE GREW AND THE DESKTOP DID NOT, WHICH IS NOT OBVIOUS
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Measured: +67/68px on 390 with every cut CLOSED, +0 on 2560, 1920 and
1440 with every cut closed.

HYPOTHESIS, NOT VERIFIED. Three nodes now carry a longer state line -
`not measured here - its step is in Actions, not in a timeline` where
they used to carry `not run yet` - so each wraps to more lines. All
three are ALONE in their phase (ECR push in Build, migrate + seed in
Provision, the human gate in Approve), and on a desktop the map's row
height is set by the tallest phase in the row, which is stage-apply with
seven nodes. So the growth is absorbed there and shows up directly on
the phone, where the map is one column.

What would settle it: measure the three phases' own heights either side,
rather than the document's. That is the same move 20a's lesson already
demands - ask the box about its own container - and it is left to the
session that does the packing, which will be measuring phase heights
anyway.
